WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:06.430
Somewhere tonight, in the Verizon center in
Washington DC, magic will happen.

00:00:06.430 --> 00:00:07.509
Maybe not here.

00:00:07.509 --> 00:00:12.550
But maybe here, or here, or here. And definitely
here.

00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:17.609
The kiss cam's magic doesn't happen by chance.
They have to select the kissers, keep a few

00:00:17.609 --> 00:00:23.259
secrets, and work an arena crowd, not just
a couple. The kiss cam is the story of a high-tech

00:00:23.259 --> 00:00:27.359
theatrical production and a business model,
falling in love.

00:00:27.359 --> 00:00:33.100
A few decks above the court is a guy locked
into a headset.

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:38.149
Zak Grim's the manager of
game entertainment.

00:00:38.149 --> 00:00:43.010
"Anything that happens in the arena bowl on
a game night that is not the game of basketball

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:44.260
is kind of my domain."

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:47.809
That means he's cutting through the activity
of a game night to find the right couples.

00:00:47.809 --> 00:00:51.710
"We are the ones that kind of execute it.
So we create all the graphics that go around

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:56.559
it, we're on headset trying to pick out where
all the couples are in the crowd, saying 'Oh,

00:00:56.559 --> 00:01:00.019
section 220 looks like it's got a lot of good
people in it. Put a camera on that, let's

00:01:00.019 --> 00:01:02.839
find a couple there.' So we're the ones actually
executing it."

00:01:02.839 --> 00:01:07.100
And Zak's always connected to somebody in
the windowless control room on the ground

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:12.720
floor — somebody who's put a president and
the first lady on the kiss cam.

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:16.320
"I was the one who did that, yes."

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:21.729
Quentin, Q for short, has a feed of every
camera constantly ready, and he's locked into

00:01:21.729 --> 00:01:27.880
cameramen who can give him options. He cuts
between them as Zak fills each discrete programming

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:32.490
segment, from the Wizard Girls, to the money
machine, to the kiss cam, making the whole

00:01:32.490 --> 00:01:35.840
night a production with a ton of moving parts.

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:40.450
All that effort only makes sense because the
kiss cam isn't an accident — it's a business

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:43.719
model made for modern sports.

00:01:43.719 --> 00:01:48.570
The history of the kiss cam is recent, but
hazy. Some people credit the Dodgers, others

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:53.640
think the Marlins came up with it at some
point in the early 90s. And it makes sense,

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:59.409
because nobody knew kiss cams would become...a
phenomenon. But, in some ways, they were a

00:01:59.409 --> 00:02:01.530
foregone conclusion.

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:07.140
Arenas have big incentives to maximize revenue
in the facility. That money's often kept in

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:12.770
a different pot from the NBA and sometimes
the arena and team are separate entities.

00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:18.300
So that's why you see a bevy of sponsored
fan packages, sponsored blimps, LED wraparounds

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:22.850
courtesy of large banks, and, though basketball
fans are passionate about the folk dances

00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:27.520
of the Republic of Turkey, you're probably
only seeing it thanks to a check from Etihad

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:28.240
Airlines.

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:33.310
And that's why the kiss cam is sponsored too.
Videoboards —&nbsp;Jumbotron's the branded term

00:02:33.310 --> 00:02:37.000
— are a big and shiny example of arenas'
profit centers.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:42.410
"They are powerful sales tools in serving
ads to fans, basically, and they're also part

00:02:42.410 --> 00:02:49.070
of sponsorship deals. Because of the location,
fans are a captive audience and they are amazingly

00:02:49.070 --> 00:02:51.880
effective at getting the attention of people
in the arena.

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:56.730
And that's one reason they put so much work
into making the kiss cam click. If a couple

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:59.120
doesn't kiss, that's not a bad thing.

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:03.910
"We'll come back to them."
"Hold on, we're gonna come back."

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:09.040
Whatever makes for a good show is a good kiss.

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:16.320
"Go back."
"Go back. See...there you go."

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:21.590
The kiss cam is part of a sponsored package
with two audiences — the fans, and the people

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:23.510
who pay for it.

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:26.380
"Let's go to our people, Q."

00:03:26.380 --> 00:03:27.960
The occasional plant happens too.

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:31.240
"Ready to unleash."

00:03:31.240 --> 00:03:42.700
But usually, the love is legitimate. What
happens in Verizon Center is not a game. It's

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:47.360
different every time because new people want
their shot at video board glory.

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:53.590
"There you go. Oh gosh. Three underneath...dissolve."

00:03:53.590 --> 00:04:01.590
"One more after them Q, one more after them."

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:04.120
There's no referee here, just applause.

00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:12.970
"What is this usher doing?"
"He's giving them certificates. OK, let 'em

00:04:12.970 --> 00:04:19.609
kiss. We're gonna stay with them. Honey, honey
look!"

00:04:19.609 --> 00:04:21.819
"Beautiful. Fade music."

00:04:21.819 --> 00:04:23.300
"Go clean."

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:27.729
"Great way to end it, perfect."

00:04:27.729 --> 00:04:32.409
It's a professional show put on by people
at the top of their field to make fans happy

00:04:32.409 --> 00:04:34.300
and bring in a lot of cash.

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:37.289
Oh. There's a basketball game too.

00:04:37.289 --> 00:04:42.490
"One of the workers came and asked if we would
do this little skit on the kiss cam."

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:45.750
"All we had to do was be prepared for her
to be pulled out of the camera and there'd

00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:50.730
be a lot of silly string. She thought he was
furry and cute, so I was like, I hope he doesn't

00:04:50.730 --> 00:04:52.390
steal my girl."

